{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'git show --format=fuller --find-renames e6522ceb -- src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc src/cljc/yang/clojure/prelude.cljc test/yang/clojure_callsite_test.cljc'","aggregated_output":"git: warning: confstr() failed with code 5: couldn't get path of DARWIN_USER_TEMP_DIR; using /tmp instead\ngit: error: couldn't create cache file '/tmp/xcrun_db-NbRUoAlg' (errno=Operation not permitted)\n2026-11-07 01:47:16.400 xcodebuild[40890:113211647]  DVTFilePathFSEvents: Failed to start fs event stream.\n2026-11-07 01:47:16.712 xcodebuild[40890:113211644] [MT] DVTDeveloperPaths: Failed to get length of DARWIN_USER_CACHE_DIR from confstr(3), error = Error Domain=NSPOSIXErrorDomain Code=5 \"Input/output error\". Using NSCachesDirectory instead.\ngit: warning: confstr() failed with code 5: couldn't get path of DARWIN_USER_TEMP_DIR; using /tmp instead\ngit: error: couldn't create cache file '/tmp/xcrun_db-Y204MViA' (errno=Operation not permitted)\n2026-11-07 01:47:17.540 xcodebuild[40897:113211700]  DVTFilePathFSEvents: Failed to start fs event stream.\n2026-11-07 01:47:17.737 xcodebuild[40897:113211697] [MT] DVTDeveloperPaths: Failed to get length of DARWIN_USER_CACHE_DIR from confstr(3), error = Error Domain=NSPOSIXErrorDomain Code=5 \"Input/output error\". Using NSCachesDirectory instead.\ncommit e6522ceb390cd8481f1137f136eeaca0b98b3199\nAuthor:     Sonny To <son.c.to@gmail.com>\nAuthorDate: Fri Nov 6 23:16:17 2026 +0700\nCommit:     Sonny To <son.c.to@gmail.com>\nCommitDate: Fri Nov 6 23:16:17 2026 +0700\n\n    feat(yang.clojure): the C1 call-site occurrence contract (Addendum A round 1)\n    \n    Every final :application occurrence of a production yang.clojure tree\n    carries the reserved :yang/call-site 1 frontend-metadata key, projected\n    into the side table as [origin root-address path :yang/call-site 1].\n    Finalization happens once over the finished tree at compile-form,\n    compile-program, lower-unit, and the clj prelude module tree; yin/def\n    occurrences are marked, dedicated stream/continuation nodes never are,\n    and :yang/site safepoint marks are untouched. Canonical rows and roots\n    are unchanged (the key drops at projection).\n    \n    validate-call-site-coverage! derives the eligible application set from\n    canonical rows and the occurrence relation and refuses conflicting\n    values, unsupported versions, nonexistent paths, non-application\n    targets, and incomplete coverage under a C1 claim; duplicate identical\n    deliveries dedupe.\n\ndiff --git a/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc b/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc\nindex a59c1122..c50abeab 100644\n--- a/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc\n+++ b/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc\n@@ -43,6 +43,147 @@\n (declare compile-form compile-lambda)\n \n \n+;; =============================================================================\n+;; Call-site occurrence contract C1 (Addendum A, design §2)\n+;; =============================================================================\n+;;\n+;; Every final `:application` occurrence of a produced tree carries the\n+;; reserved frontend-metadata key `:yang/call-site` with version value `1`\n+;; as a plain node key. Projection (`yin.vm/ast-side-tables`) drops the key\n+;; from canonical rows and emits it into the frontend-metadata side table\n+;; as `[origin root-address path :yang/call-site 1]`, where the first\n+;; three coordinates are the site id. The key carries no callee identity,\n+;; source arity, or ambient classification. It is distinct from\n+;; `:yang/site`, the safepoint mark, which travels as node metadata.\n+;; Dedicated node kinds (`:dao.stream.apply/call`, stream and\n+;; continuation nodes) are not `:application` nodes and are never marked.\n+\n+(def call-site-key\n+  \"The reserved frontend-metadata key of contract C1.\"\n+  :yang/call-site)\n+\n+\n+(def call-site-version\n+  \"The version value a C1 marker carries.\"\n+  1)\n+\n+\n+(def ^:private ^:dynamic *call-site-finalizing*\n+  \"True while an owning production entry point compiles a tree, so the\n+   recursive `compile-form` calls inside it defer marking to that entry\n+   point's single finalization walk over the finished tree.\"\n+  false)\n+\n+\n+(defn annotate-call-sites\n+  \"The finished map AST `node` with `call-site-key`/`call-site-version`\n+   on every `:application` node, at every depth the row grammar knows.\n+   Literal payloads are data, never syntax, and are not walked. Marking\n+   is idempotent and preserves node metadata and every other key, so\n+   canonical rows, roots, and executable outcomes are unchanged.\"\n+  [node]\n+  (let [tag (:type node)\n+        slots (get vm/semantic-bytecode-grammar tag)]\n+    (when-not slots\n+      (throw (ex-info \"Unknown AST node type\" {:type tag, :node node})))\n+    (let [walked (reduce (fn [n [field kind]]\n+                           (case kind\n+                             :node (update n field annotate-call-sites)\n+                             :nodes (update n field\n+                                            (fn [children]\n+                                              (mapv annotate-call-sites\n+                                                    children)))\n+                             n))\n+                         node\n+                         slots)]\n+      (cond-> walked\n+        (= :application tag) (assoc call-site-key call-site-version)))))\n+\n+\n+(defn eligible-application-sites\n+  \"The eligible C1 site set of canonical `tree` (`{:root :rows}`) under\n+   `origin`: one `[origin root-address path]` per `:application`\n+   occurrence, derived from the occurrence relation and the row tags.\"\n+  [tree origin]\n+  (let [{:keys [root rows]} tree]\n+    (into #{}\n+          (comp (filter (fn [[_ _ id]] (= :application (nth (get rows id) 1))))\n+                (map (fn [[_ path _]] [origin root path])))\n+          (vm/occurrences tree))))\n+\n+\n+(defn marked-application-sites\n+  \"The deduped C1 marker set of a frontend-metadata relation: one\n+   `[origin root-address path]` per distinct `:yang/call-site` row.\n+   Duplicate identical transport deliveries dedupe to the same fact.\"\n+  [frontend-metadata]\n+  (into #{}\n+        (comp (filter (fn [row]\n+                        (and (= 5 (count row)) (= call-site-key (nth row 3)))))\n+              (map (fn [[origin root path _ _]] [origin root path])))\n+        (distinct frontend-metadata)))\n+\n+\n+(defn validate-call-site-coverage!\n+  \"Validate a complete-coverage C1 claim: the marker set of\n+   `frontend-metadata` for canonical `tree` under `origin` must equal\n+   the eligible application set. Returns true when the claim holds.\n+   Conflicting values at one site, an unsupported marker version, a\n+   marker naming no occurrence, a marker on a non-application\n+   occurrence, and missing or extra markers each throw, naming the\n+   failed `:rule`.\"\n+  [tree frontend-metadata origin]\n+  (let [{:keys [root rows]} tree\n+        tag-at (into {}\n+                     (map (fn [[r path id]] [[r path] (nth (get rows id) 1)]))\n+                     (vm/occurrences tree))\n+        eligible (eligible-application-sites tree origin)\n+        rows (filter (fn [row]\n+                       (and (= 5 (count row)) (= call-site-key (nth row 3))))\n+                     (distinct frontend-metadata))\n+        by-site (group-by (fn [[o r path _ _]] [o r path]) rows)]\n+    (doseq [[site srows] by-site]\n+      (when (< 1 (count (distinct (map #(nth % 4) srows))))\n+        (throw (ex-info \"Conflicting call-site marker values\"\n+                        {:rule :yang/call-site-conflict, :site site,\n+                         :values (vec (distinct (map #(nth % 4) srows)))}))))\n+    (doseq [[o r path _ value] rows]\n+      (when (not= call-site-version value)\n+        (throw (ex-info \"Unsupported call-site marker version\"\n+                        {:rule :yang/call-site-unsupported-version,\n+                         :site [o r path], :value value})))\n+      (let [tag (when (and (= o origin) (= r root)) (get tag-at [r path]))]\n+        (cond\n+          (nil? tag)\n+          (throw (ex-info \"Call-site marker names no occurrence\"\n+                          {:rule :yang/call-site-nonexistent-path,\n+                           :site [o r path]}))\n+          (not= :application tag)\n+          (throw (ex-info \"Call-site marker on a non-application occurrence\"\n+                          {:rule :yang/call-site-non-application,\n+                           :site [o r path], :tag tag})))))\n+    (let [marked (marked-application-sites frontend-metadata)]\n+      (when (not= eligible marked)\n+        (throw (ex-info \"Call-site coverage is not complete\"\n+                        {:rule :yang/call-site-incomplete-coverage,\n+                         :missing (vec (sort-by pr-str\n+                                                (remove marked eligible))),\n+                         :extra (vec (sort-by pr-str\n+                                              (remove eligible marked)))}))))\n+    true))\n+\n+\n+(defn validate-ast-call-sites!\n+  \"Validate the C1 claim of a produced map AST `ast` under `origin`:\n+   project it and compare the eligible application set derived from its\n+   canonical rows with the marker set of its frontend-metadata side\n+   table. Returns true when the sets are equal.\"\n+  [ast origin]\n+  (let [tree (vm/ast->semantic-bytecode ast)\n+        tables (vm/ast-side-tables ast tree origin)]\n+    (validate-call-site-coverage! tree (:frontend-metadata tables) origin)))\n+\n+\n (defn literal?\n   \"Check if a value is a literal (self-evaluating).\"\n   [form]\n@@ -2015,20 +2156,30 @@\n                                     :default (clojure.core/type form))}))))\n \n \n+(defn- compile-form-1\n+  [form tail? env macro-env]\n+  (let [ast (compile-form* form tail? (dissoc env ::top-level) macro-env\n+                           (::top-level env))\n+        m (meta form)]\n+    (if (seq (dissoc m ::fn-loop))\n+      (vary-meta ast merge (dissoc m ::fn-loop))\n+      ast)))\n+\n+\n (defn compile-form\n   \"Compile one Clojure form and retain the reader's plain metadata on the\n    emitted Universal AST node. The tuple boundary removes it from content\n-   and writes positions and other frontend facts to occurrence side tables.\"\n+   and writes positions and other frontend facts to occurrence side tables.\n+   The returned tree is C1-finalized (`annotate-call-sites`); recursive\n+   calls inside one compilation defer to the owning call's walk.\"\n   ([form] (compile-form form false {} initial-macro-env))\n   ([form env] (compile-form form false env initial-macro-env))\n   ([form tail? env] (compile-form form tail? env initial-macro-env))\n   ([form tail? env macro-env]\n-   (let [ast (compile-form* form tail? (dissoc env ::top-level) macro-env\n-                            (::top-level env))\n-         m (meta form)]\n-     (if (seq (dissoc m ::fn-loop))\n-       (vary-meta ast merge (dissoc m ::fn-loop))\n-       ast))))\n+   (if *call-site-finalizing*\n+     (compile-form-1 form tail? env macro-env)\n+     (binding [*call-site-finalizing* true]\n+       (annotate-call-sites (compile-form-1 form tail? env macro-env))))))\n \n \n (defn- top-level-defined-fns\n@@ -2225,7 +2376,8 @@\n                                            (compile-form head false\n                                                          (assoc env ::top-level true) macro-env))]}\n                        tail? (assoc :tail? true))))))]\n-       (cond->> (go forms initial-macro-env)\n+       (annotate-call-sites\n+         (cond->> (go forms initial-macro-env)\n          ;; The two sibling closures share one frame: separate bindings would\n          ;; retain one extra helper environment in every closure a guest\n          ;; captures (the machine-data validation bound notices).\n@@ -2390,7 +2542,7 @@\n                                         (assoc m k v k2 v2)\n                                         (assoc m k v k2 v2 k3 v3))))))\n                              (u/sexp->uast '(fn [xs] (data/content= 0 (data/count xs))))))\n-         (outcomes? env) u/mark-tails)))))\n+           (outcomes? env) u/mark-tails))))))\n \n \n ;; =============================================================================\n@@ -3017,7 +3169,10 @@\n                              (concat (map (comp strip-symbol-meta second) library)\n                                      (map symbol exports)))\n                        macros)]\n-     (u/lam [] (publish-to-globals program names #{})))))\n+     ;; `publish-to-globals` rewrites nodes after `compile-program`\n+     ;; finalized them, so the unit is finalized again over its\n+     ;; finished tree: the rewrite's own applications are occurrences.\n+     (annotate-call-sites (u/lam [] (publish-to-globals program names #{}))))))\n \n \n (defn output\ndiff --git a/src/cljc/yang/clojure/prelude.cljc b/src/cljc/yang/clojure/prelude.cljc\nindex 42a3bead..54d1a80b 100644\n--- a/src/cljc/yang/clojure/prelude.cljc\n+++ b/src/cljc/yang/clojure/prelude.cljc\n@@ -107,8 +107,9 @@\n \n (def module-uast\n   \"The module tree: one wide application over the definitions, so every\n-   sibling and runtime key read is discharged at module level.\"\n-  (core/module-tree module-definitions []))\n+   sibling and runtime key read is discharged at module level. C1\n+   finalized, like every production `yang.clojure` tree.\"\n+  (yang/annotate-call-sites (core/module-tree module-definitions [])))\n \n \n (def module-exports\ndiff --git a/test/yang/clojure_callsite_test.cljc b/test/yang/clojure_callsite_test.cljc\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 00000000..fc07410d\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/test/yang/clojure_callsite_test.cljc\n@@ -0,0 +1,193 @@\n+(ns yang.clojure-callsite-test\n+  \"Contract C1 for production yang.clojure (Addendum A, design §2): the\n+   `:yang/call-site 1` frontend-metadata annotation of every final\n+   `:application` occurrence, and the complete-coverage validation a\n+   consumer runs against canonical rows.\"\n+  (:require [clojure.test :refer [deftest is testing]]\n+            [yang.clojure :as yang]\n+            [yang.clojure.prelude]\n+            [yang.safepoint :as safepoint]\n+            [yin.vm :as vm]\n+            [yin.vm.encoder :as encoder]))\n+\n+\n+(def ^:private origin [:source :program \"batch-1\" 0])\n+\n+\n+(defn- project\n+  [ast]\n+  (let [projected (encoder/project\n+                    (encoder/source-envelope :program \"batch-1\" [ast]))]\n+    {:tree (first (:yin/batch projected))\n+     :metadata (:yin/frontend-metadata projected)}))\n+\n+\n+(defn- eligible\n+  \"The eligible set, derived here directly from canonical rows and the\n+   occurrence relation, independently of the producer's own helpers.\"\n+  [tree]\n+  (into #{}\n+        (comp (filter (fn [[_ _ id]]\n+                        (= :application (nth (get (:rows tree) id) 1))))\n+              (map (fn [[_ path _]] [origin (:root tree) path])))\n+        (vm/occurrences tree)))\n+\n+\n+(defn- marked\n+  [metadata]\n+  (into #{}\n+        (comp (filter #(= :yang/call-site (nth % 3)))\n+              (map (fn [[o r path _ _]] [o r path])))\n+        metadata))\n+\n+\n+(defn- failure-rule\n+  [f]\n+  (try (f) ::no-failure\n+       (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Exception :cljs :default) e\n+         (:rule (ex-data e)))))\n+\n+\n+(deftest equality-gate-test\n+  (testing \"native compile: eligible set equals marker set\"\n+    (let [ast (yang/compile '(+ (* 2 3) 4))\n+          {:keys [tree metadata]} (project ast)]\n+      (is (= #{[origin (:root tree) []]\n+               [origin (:root tree) [[3 0]]]}\n+             (marked metadata)))\n+      (is (= (eligible tree) (marked metadata)))\n+      (is (true? (yang/validate-call-site-coverage! tree metadata origin)))\n+      (is (true? (yang/validate-ast-call-sites! ast origin)))\n+      (is (every? (fn [[o r _ k v]]\n+                    (and (= origin o) (= (:root tree) r)\n+                         (= :yang/call-site k) (= 1 v)))\n+                  (filter #(= :yang/call-site (nth % 3)) metadata)))))\n+  (testing \"compile-program, native and argument-vector/outcome paths\"\n+    (doseq [ast [(yang/compile-program\n+                   '[(defn f [x] (+ x 1)) (defn g [x] (f (* x 2))) (g 21)])\n+                 (yang/compile-program\n+                   '[(defn f [x] (+ x 1)) (f 2)] true yang/unit-opts)]]\n+      (let [{:keys [tree metadata]} (project ast)]\n+        (is (= (eligible tree) (marked metadata)))\n+        (is (true? (yang/validate-call-site-coverage! tree metadata origin))))))\n+  (testing \"lower-unit: the linked production path, library included\"\n+    (let [ast (yang/lower-unit '[(defn f [x] (+ x 1)) (f 2)])\n+          {:keys [tree metadata]} (project ast)]\n+      (is (< 10 (count (marked metadata))))\n+      (is (= (eligible tree) (marked metadata)))\n+      (is (true? (yang/validate-call-site-coverage! tree metadata origin)))))\n+  (testing \"the clj prelude module tree is finalized\"\n+    (let [ast yang.clojure.prelude/module-uast\n+          {:keys [tree metadata]} (project ast)]\n+      (is (= (eligible tree) (marked metadata)))\n+      (is (true? (yang/validate-call-site-coverage! tree metadata origin))))))\n+\n+\n+(deftest boundary-test\n+  (testing \"yin/def gets an occurrence annotation\"\n+    (let [ast (yang/compile '(def x (fn [a] (+ a 1))))]\n+      (is (= 1 (:yang/call-site ast)))\n+      (is (= 1 (get-in ast [:operands 1 :body :yang/call-site])))\n+      (is (true? (yang/validate-ast-call-sites! ast origin)))))\n+  (testing \"a dedicated stream operation is not an application site\"\n+    (let [ast (yang/compile '(dao.stream.apply/call :op/echo (+ 1 2)))\n+          {:keys [tree metadata]} (project ast)]\n+      (is (= :dao.stream.apply/call (:type ast)))\n+      (is (not (contains? ast :yang/call-site)))\n+      ;; its operand application is an ordinary occurrence and is marked\n+      (is (= #{[origin (:root tree) [[3 0]]]} (marked metadata)))\n+      (is (true? (yang/validate-call-site-coverage! tree metadata origin)))))\n+  (testing \"stream and continuation nodes are never marked\"\n+    (let [ast (yang/annotate-call-sites\n+                {:type :application\n+                 :operator {:type :variable :name 'f}\n+                 :operands [{:type :stream/make :buffer 1}\n+                            {:type :vm/current-continuation}]})]\n+      (is (= 1 (:yang/call-site ast)))\n+      (is (not (contains? (first (:operands ast)) :yang/call-site)))\n+      (is (not (contains? (second (:operands ast)) :yang/call-site)))))\n+  (testing \"generated trees carry an expansion origin honestly\"\n+    (let [ast (yang/compile-program '[(defn f [x] (+ x 1)) (f 2)]\n+                                    true yang/unit-opts)\n+          tree (vm/ast->semantic-bytecode ast)\n+          expansion-origin [:expansion (:root tree)]]\n+      (is (true? (yang/validate-ast-call-sites! ast expansion-origin))))))\n+\n+\n+(deftest validation-failure-test\n+  (let [ast (yang/compile '(+ (* 2 3) 4))\n+        {:keys [tree metadata]} (project ast)\n+        markers (filterv #(= :yang/call-site (nth % 3)) metadata)\n+        site (vec (take 3 (first markers)))]\n+    (testing \"duplicate identical deliveries dedupe\"\n+      (is (true? (yang/validate-call-site-coverage!\n+                   tree (into metadata markers) origin))))\n+    (testing \"a conflicting value at one site fails\"\n+      (is (= :yang/call-site-conflict\n+             (failure-rule\n+               #(yang/validate-call-site-coverage!\n+                  tree (conj metadata (conj site :yang/call-site 2))\n+                  origin)))))\n+    (testing \"an unsupported version fails\"\n+      (is (= :yang/call-site-unsupported-version\n+             (failure-rule\n+               #(yang/validate-call-site-coverage!\n+                  tree (mapv (fn [row]\n+                               (if (= :yang/call-site (nth row 3))\n+                                 (assoc row 4 2) row))\n+                             metadata)\n+                  origin)))))\n+    (testing \"a nonexistent path fails\"\n+      (is (= :yang/call-site-nonexistent-path\n+             (failure-rule\n+               #(yang/validate-call-site-coverage!\n+                  tree (conj metadata [origin (:root tree) [99]\n+                                       :yang/call-site 1])\n+                  origin)))))\n+    (testing \"a non-application target fails\"\n+      ;; [[3 0] [3 0]] is the literal `2` inside `(* 2 3)`\n+      (is (= :yang/call-site-non-application\n+             (failure-rule\n+               #(yang/validate-call-site-coverage!\n+                  tree (conj metadata [origin (:root tree) [[3 0] [3 0]]\n+                                       :yang/call-site 1])\n+                  origin)))))\n+    (testing \"a missing marker under a complete-coverage claim fails\"\n+      (is (= :yang/call-site-incomplete-coverage\n+             (failure-rule\n+               #(yang/validate-call-site-coverage!\n+                  tree (vec (remove (set markers) metadata)) origin)))))))\n+\n+\n+(deftest safepoint-independence-test\n+  (testing \":yang/site marks and :yang/call-site markers are distinct\"\n+    (let [ast (yang/annotate-call-sites\n+                (vary-meta (yang/compile '(fn [x] (inc x)))\n+                           assoc :yang/site :call))\n+          tree (vm/ast->semantic-bytecode ast)\n+          tables (vm/ast-side-tables ast tree origin)]\n+      (is (= {[] :call}\n+             (safepoint/sites (:frontend-metadata tables) origin (:root tree))))\n+      (is (true? (yang/validate-call-site-coverage!\n+                   tree (:frontend-metadata tables) origin)))\n+      (is (not-any? (fn [[_ _ _ k _]] (= :yang/site k))\n+                    (filter #(= :yang/call-site (nth % 3))\n+                            (:frontend-metadata tables)))))))\n+\n+\n+(deftest canonical-invariance-test\n+  (testing \"marking changes no canonical row, root, or outcome input\"\n+    (let [form '(defn f [x] (+ (* x 2) 1))\n+          marked (yang/compile-program [form '(f 21)])\n+          strip (fn strip [node]\n+                  (let [slots (get vm/semantic-bytecode-grammar (:type node))]\n+                    (reduce (fn [n [field kind]]\n+                              (case kind\n+                                :node (update n field strip)\n+                                :nodes (update n field\n+                                               #(mapv strip %))\n+                                n))\n+                            (dissoc node :yang/call-site)\n+                            slots)))]\n+      (is (= (vm/ast->semantic-bytecode (strip marked))\n+             (vm/ast->semantic-bytecode marked))))))\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
