 178\t   project it and compare the eligible application set derived from its\n   179\t   canonical rows with the marker set of its frontend-metadata side\n   180\t   table. Returns true when the sets are equal.\"\n   181\t  [ast origin]\n   182\t  (let [tree (vm/ast->semantic-bytecode ast)\n   183\t        tables (vm/ast-side-tables ast tree origin)]\n   184\t    (validate-call-site-coverage! tree (:frontend-metadata tables) origin)))\n   185\t\n  2300\t  form)\n  2301\t\n  2302\t\n  2303\t(defn- lower-top-form\n  2304\t  \"Under the outcome model a top-level expression returns an outcome like a\n  2305\t   function body; definitions keep their own lowering.\"\n  2306\t  [env macro-env form]\n  2307\t  (if (and (seq? form) (contains? #{'def 'defn 'defn- 'defmacro} (first form)))\n  2308\t    form\n  2309\t    (lower-function-body env macro-env [] [form])))\n  2310\t\n  2311\t\n  2312\t(defn compile-program\n  2313\t  \"Compile a sequence of Clojure forms into a single Universal AST.\n  2314\t   Top-level defs compile to explicit yin/def store writes, sequenced via lambda.\n  2315\t   Top-level defmacros are lowered to ordinary (yin/def name (fn ...)) syntax\n  2316\t   with :macro? true on the lambda; the encoder turns that flag into a\n  2317\t   declaration row and the expander, not this compiler, recognizes calls.\n  2318\t   The three-argument form takes `opts` opting into the argument-vector\n  2319\t   convention (see `program-env`); without it the output is the native one.\"\n  2320\t  ([forms] (compile-program forms true))\n  2321\t  ([forms tail?] (compile-program forms tail? nil))\n  2322\t  ([forms tail? opts]\n  2323\t   (run! check-program-symbols! forms)\n  2324\t   (let [env (program-env forms opts)]\n  2325\t     ;; A discarded definition must not become a lexical binding in the\n  2326\t     ;; following definitions. Descriptor entry and body closures both capture\n  2327\t     ;; their environment: retaining the previous descriptor here doubles it