{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_21","type":"agent_message","text":"**REJECT for landing at `e6522ceb`.** The map-AST annotation is substantial and the equality tests are meaningful, but the production paths do not yet preserve C1 markers through expansion and publication.\n\n1. **The REPL loses markers before the final expanded tree exists.** [repl.cljc](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cc1/src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc:1652) passes the compiled AST to `encoder/program-batch`, which emits canonical rows without frontend metadata ([encoder.cljc](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cc1/src/cljc/yin/vm/encoder.cljc:241)). The expander then produces a new final tree after tail marking and stand-in lowering ([macro.cljc](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cc1/src/cljc/yin/vm/macro.cljc:1255)), with no C1 finalization or side table for that tree. The current tests project compiler-returned maps before this production pipeline, so they cannot establish post-expansion coverage.\n\n2. **Linked publication drops the prelude’s markers.** [prelude.cljc](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cc1/src/cljc/yang/clojure/prelude.cljc:108) annotates `module-uast`, but [publish.cljc](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cc1/src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/publish.cljc:117) converts the AST directly to canonical rows and publishes the code closure without extracting or retaining frontend metadata. Thus the test that projects `module-uast` does not demonstrate markers are available from the published module. The design explicitly includes published `clj` and `yang.call` coverage.\n\n3. **The validator does not implement all of §2.2’s refusal rules.** [clojure.cljc](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cc1/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc:141) silently filters malformed marker rows and unconditionally deduplicates identical rows. A malformed extra marker can therefore be ignored, and duplicate entries in a declared canonical table cannot be distinguished from duplicate transport deliveries. The contract permits deduplication of the latter but requires rejection of the former. The named conflict, version, path, non-application, and missing-coverage tests do exercise their respective branches.\n\n4. **Required acceptance evidence remains incomplete.** The design requires Clojure publication/load/query and trace fixtures across JVM, Node, Dart, and Jolt, plus cross-host occurrence-key equality. The quoted results establish the callsite battery and oracle consumer check on the reported host; they do not establish those mandatory gates. The frontend catalog also retains revision `legacy-1` ([frontends.cljc](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cc1/src/cljc/yin/repl/frontends.cljc:26)), despite the design requiring a revision and relevant profile change when the coverage promise changes.\n\nThe reviewed marker walk uses grammar-defined child paths, keeps the marker out of canonical rows, and distinguishes it from `:yang/site`. The equality and boundary tests are non-vacuous for the map ASTs they exercise. One test labels `[:expansion (:root tree)]` as an expansion origin ([clojure_callsite_test.cljc](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cc1/test/yang/clojure_callsite_test.cljc:109)); that checks the accepted shape, not a real expansion-record address.\n\nThe reported CBOR stream failure is a separate, pre-existing test and no stream file is in this commit’s diff. That supports its attribution for investigation, but does not by itself prove the failure is unrelated. The Node run also timed out, so it is not a completed green lane.\n\nThis was a static review; I did not run suites. The remote results are cited as supplied."}}
